      "lineNbr": 3480,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003935
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-08-27T13:03:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Calling newCommit.getShortMessage() works before calling\nReachabilityChecker#areAllReachable and fails with an NPE afterwards. The NPE is because buffer in RevCommit is null now. Calling parseBody populates it again.\n\n```\n/**\n * Raw unparsed commit body of the commit. Populated only\n * after {@link #parseCanonical(RevWalk, byte[])} with\n * {@link RevWalk#isRetainBody()} enable or after\n * {@link #parseBody(RevWalk)} and {@link #parse(RevWalk, byte[])}.\n *\n * @since 6.5.1\n */\nprotected byte[] buffer;\n```\n\t\nYes, I think this is a bug that should be fix in JGit.",
      "parentUuid": "470f8aa5_db9ae00d",
      "revId": "df05f8560b555af5a712ede35e0ac8ad514edef9",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
